UPSTREAM.toml is the machine-readable version of the same thing: source commit, upstream
path, local status, and for anything vendored unchanged, the SHA-256 of the file. A test
verifies those hashes, so a local edit to a vendored file fails the build until it is
reclassified as adapted.


